   "args": {
    "summary": "Model repaired and passing all checks.\n\nROOT CAUSE OF FAILURE\nThe static analysis failed with \"matrix singular\" / \"aii < 0 (180)\" because the structure had no longitudinal stiffness anywhere. Support 1 (Pier 1, plain non-sliding laminated elastomeric bearings) had been decided as support.1.dofs = {longitudinal: \"free\"}, while all three other support lines are PTFE sliding (Kh = 0, longitudinal free). With every support line longitudinally free, the assembled stiffness matrix was singular in the longitudinal direction.\n\nFIX\nPer modeling rule MR-03 (板式橡胶支座的模拟): a plain laminated elastomeric bearing takes the shear stiffness Kh as a longitudinal SPRING (\"普通板式支座纵向取剪切刚度 Kh\"), only sliding (PTFE) bearings are longitudinally free. I revised support.1.dofs to {vertical: \"spring\", longitudinal: \"spring\", rotation: \"free\"} with evidence MR-03. This is consistent with the already-accepted support.1.Kh = 26250 kN/m.\n\nMODEL SUMMARY (as regenerated)\n- Three-span continuous spine-beam model, 20 + 25 + 20 m, precast small-box girders (4 per span), C50, self-weight 110.29 kN/m per girder.\n- Continuous system over 4 support lines: abutment 0, pier 1, pier 2, abutment 3.\n- Bearings: PTFE sliding at supports 0, 2, 3 (longitudinally free); plain laminated elastomeric at support 1 (longitudinal spring Kh = 26.25 MN/m); all vertical on springs Kv = 11.33 MN/m.\n- Design loading: Highway Class I, 3 lanes, one-way, ξ = 0.78, qk = 10.5 kN/m, Pk = 300/310/300 kN; impact factor μ = 0.2879 from f1 = 5.573 Hz.\n\nKEY RESULTS\n- First three vertical frequencies: 5.573, 8.426, 10.186 Hz (f1 unchanged from the modal run).\n- Self-weight reactions: abutments 820.5 kN each, piers 2764.1 kN each.\n- Lane-load max positive moment 5341.5 kNm (mid span 2); max negative moment −3864.0 kNm (at interior supports)."
   },
